From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:25:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Radio: apply MLD changes before syncing the radio
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MLDUnitSetting changes the per-AP mld_ap and disable_11be parameters,
but its handler only requests a radio sync. The generic plugin then
schedules DISABLE and ENABLE without GEN_FSM_MOD_MLD, so its existing
MLD re-add handling cannot replace the toggle. Writing the new config
file does not update the MLD layout still loaded in hostapd.

On a transition from Assumed to Required with no SSID MLDUnit, ENABLE
starts the old MLD layout before the subsequent config reload:

  wlan0.1: interface state DISABLED->COUNTRY_UPDATE
  Failed to set beacon parameters

Notify each AP through the existing setMldUnit callback before
requesting the radio sync. This queues the same MLD action as an
SSID.MLDUnit edit. The generic FSM can then replace the toggle with a
config re-add when an MLD is running or expected, and check per-AP MLD
changes before writing the new config. The radio auto-commit covers the
AP actions as well.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/wld_radio.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/wld_radio.c b/src/wld_radio.c
index e08c170b2a6a..c912a9275da0 100644
--- a/src/wld_radio.c
+++ b/src/wld_radio.c
@@ -5393,6 +5393,13 @@ static void s_setMLDUnitSetting_pwf(void* priv _UNUSED, amxd_object_t* object, a
 
     if(pR->mldUnitSetting != newVal) {
         pR->mldUnitSetting = newVal;
+        /* Apply per-AP MLD changes before the radio sync can enable hostapd. */
+        T_AccessPoint* pAP = NULL;
+        wld_rad_forEachAp(pAP, pR) {
+            if(pAP->pSSID != NULL) {
+                pAP->pFA->mfn_wvap_setMldUnit(pAP);
+            }
+        }
         wld_rad_doSync(pR);
         wld_rad_setAllMldLinksUnconfigured(pR);
     }
